1. d4 {... 0-1, 50 moves. Charles Wreford-Brown (1866-1951) played the first
two rounds of the 1933 British Championship but was then taken sick. His place
was taken by Alfred Mortlock, who subsequently played the same two opponents
that Wreford-Brown had played in the first two rounds and completed a full
schedule of games.} 0-1

